id: pm-zod466
title: Remediate independent-feed development dependency advisories
description: Fresh independent registry/OSV security checks on 2026-10-24 identify GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5 in Zod and additional fast-uri and Undici findings that the registry alone misses. Consolidate compatible security floors at the existing workspace override boundary; retain all feed evidence and require zero findings across the complete locked dependency population. No public runtime exploit path is asserted.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: dependencies,sdk,security
created_at: "2026-10-23T23:28:44.884Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T00:28:57.626Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T00:15:26.937Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T00:15:26.937Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: No installed or locked Zod copy is below4.6.6; public-registry audit and maintained dependency gates pass; typecheck and functional or mutation controls preserve development-tool and SDK behavior
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: 90
resolution: "Compatible workspace security floors consolidate Zod4.6.7, fast-uri3.1.9 and Undici6.29.1 across all active lockfile paths. Registry and OSV checks remain mandatory. Unused ext-apps embedded parser bytes are excluded from the CLI runtime/distribution and retained as a separate future-adoption constraint in pm-extapps-vendor-zod."
expected_result: "All active dependency versions clear both feeds without breaking supported APIs, engines or development tools; unshipped vendor bytes are not misrepresented as patched."
actual_result: "The unchanged567-package all-dependency gate passes with zero registry and OSV findings; frozen install, strict typecheck, Knip/development-bundle checks and valid constrained-collection controls pass. Security review found no further reachable candidate regression. The unused upstream vendor-bundle limitation remains open and unclaimed."
