comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T23:28:44.884Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: canonical orientation and current open/in_progress lists plus complete strict3083-item all-status corpus including closed history were read. Exact GHSA search found no match. Closed pm-4ydh covers a different Zod advisory and remains completed. This new report is validated by fresh registry audit and upstream advisory; no production exploit reachability is asserted."
  "2026-10-23T23:31:01.613Z","harness:codex","Independent boundary review: all Zod callers accept4.6.6+ within4.x and the override resolves4.6.7. Current MCP ext-apps usage in pm source is type-only; production exploit reachability is not established. Upstream patch bounds constrained collections before element traversal and does not cap arbitrary unbounded arrays. A second complete OSV feed reports four fast-uri3.1.8 advisories and two Undici6.28.1 advisories, while registry counts are zero. The unchanged fail-closed gate blocked correctly; inspect compatible security floors for those copies before continuing."
  "2026-10-23T23:33:27.641Z","harness:codex","Dependency fix evidence: compatible workspace floors now resolve Zod4.6.7; fast-uri3.1.9; Undici6.29.1. Parent semver ranges and Node engine floors remain satisfied. The unchanged all-lockfile advisory gate exits0 across567 packages: registry all-severity counts0 and OSV findings0. Original independent-feed failure is retained locally; no provider was suppressed and no security policy was weakened."
  "2026-10-23T23:40:32.610Z","harness:codex","Adversarial review limitation: ext-apps2.0.3 is the latest upstream release but embeds Zod4.3.5 in its app-with-deps and react-with-deps development bundles. A bounded direct probe confirms the first bundle still visits oversized-array elements. pm-cli imports ext-apps/server only as a TypeScript type; these development-only bundles have no application runtime import and are absent from the runtime dependency manifest and npm packlist. The patched lockfile and dual-feed result certify active dependency resolution; they do not certify that all installed vendor bytes are patched. Retain this upstream limitation and verify future adoption without rewriting unused third-party bundles."
  "2026-10-24T00:03:49.435Z","harness:codex","Dependency update inventory is preserved separately from security admission: GitHub has no open dependency PRs or vulnerability alerts. The registry also lists elective toolchain updates and major migrations; existing pm-do5b, pm-ksr40d and pm-t3jxjj retain the TypeScript7, npm-package-arg14 and Sentry11 compatibility work. This PR adopts only compatible security floors and does not bypass the seven-day updater cooldown, the supported Node floor or the CodSpeed artifact policy."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T23:41:23.370Z","harness:codex",An independent all-lockfile registry/OSV audit cannot inspect code embedded inside another dependency bundle. Keep resolved versions; installed bundle bytes; application reachability; and published-artifact inclusion as separate security claims.
